         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://host/fedora/services/access?wsdl,",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " and using FieldSearchQuery.conditions and Condition.@operator, property, and value combinations, the service returns \"org.xml.sax.SAXException: Found character data inside an array element while deserializing.\"  This may be an issue with the WSDL or it may be an issue with how .NET is creating the proxy class, but either way, it doesn't work. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "--------\n",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Code:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "FedoraAPIAService a = new FedoraAPIAService();",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "FieldSearchQuery fsq = new FieldSearchQuery();",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Condition c = new Condition();",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "c.@operator = ComparisonOperator.has;",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "c.property = \"subject\";",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "c.value = \"*\";",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "fsq.conditions = new Condition[] { c };",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "string[] sr = { \"pid\", \"title\", \"subject\" };",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "FieldSearchResult fsr = a.findObjects(sr, \"50\", fsq);",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "--------\n",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "When using \"terms\" it doesn't work either. Also, if I use the fedora generated WSDL, .terms and .conditions doesn't exist. There is just a .Items property.  When I pass a condition object to this, the proxy throws an in appropriate type exception.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
